  "query_preview": "CAM guidance is hinting at the southern extend of \nthunderstorms remaining north of the region. Overall, most will \nnot see rain as the heat continues to build heading into \nSunday. High temperatures may reach the mid- to upper-90s with \nheat index values near 100, marking the hottest day in some \ntime. \n\nThankfully, the aforementioned trough helps to weaken and \nflatten the ridge heading into next week. Slightly cooler \ntemperatures return, but remain above normal in the mid- to \nupper-80s. Periodic thunderstorm chances remain in the forecast\nduring this time, but confidence is low. Rain chances may \nlargely depend on the southern extent of any passing weather \ndisturbances or any mesoscale features (fronts, outflow, MCV, \netc.) that can help with thunderstorm development. As the ridge\ncontinues to flatten by mid-week, rain chances should gradually\nincrease.",
